    {
      "id": "nannu12",
      "icon": "👴",
      "title": "Talking to grandad · a chat",
      "subtitle": "Dialogue with a grandfather on how things used to be",
      "intro": "Mary asks her grandfather about old Malta. Listen for kont, it turns up in almost every line.",
      "dialogue": [
        {
          "mt": "Nannu, kif kont tmur għax-xogħol meta kont żgħir?",
          "en": "Grandad, how did you go to work when you were young?"
        },
        {
          "mt": "Kont immur bit-tramm jew bil-karozza tal-linja.",
          "en": "I used to go by tram or by bus."
        },
        {
          "mt": "U l-ferrovija kont tużaha?",
          "en": "And the railway, did you use it?"
        },
        {
          "mt": "Iva, kont nuża l-ferrovija ukoll.",
          "en": "Yes, I used to use the railway too."
        },
        {
          "mt": "Fejn kont taħdem?",
          "en": "Where did you work?"
        },
        {
          "mt": "Jien kont ħaddied.",
          "en": "I was a blacksmith."
        },
        {
          "mt": "Kont issib ħwienet tal-ħelu?",
          "en": "Were there any sweet shops?"
        },
        {
          "mt": "Iva, kont niekol ħelu kuljum!",
          "en": "Yes, I used to eat sweets every day!"
        },
        {
          "mt": "Kemm hu interessanti nisma' fuq il-passat, nannu!",
          "en": "How interesting it is to hear about the past, grandad!"
        }
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "ex3",
          "type": "build",
          "max": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "mt": "Kont immur bit-tramm jew bil-karozza tal-linja.",
              "en": "I used to go by tram or by bus."
            },
            {
              "mt": "Fejn kont taħdem?",
              "en": "Where did you work?"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Jien kont ħaddied.",
              "en": "I was a blacksmith."
            },
            {
              "mt": "Kemm hu interessanti nisma' fuq il-passat, nannu!",
              "en": "How interesting it is to hear about the past, grandad!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "kont12",
      "icon": "🕰️",
      "title": "The past of to be",
      "subtitle": "The verb kien, and how kont makes 'used to'",
      "intro": "You already know the past endings from kiteb and ħadem. The verb kien takes the same endings.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "id": "kien",
          "title": "kien (he was): the same endings you already know",
          "rows": [
            {
              "person": "Jien (I)",
              "ending": "-t",
              "form": "kont",
              "en": "I was",
              "say": "Jien kont"
            },
            {
              "person": "Int (you)",
              "ending": "-t",
              "form": "kont",
              "en": "you were",
              "say": "Int kont"
            },
            {
              "person": "Hu (he)",
              "ending": "-",
              "form": "kien",
              "en": "he was",
              "say": "Hu kien"
            },
            {
              "person": "Hi (she)",
              "ending": "-et",
              "form": "kienet",
              "en": "she was",
              "say": "Hi kienet"
            },
            {
              "person": "Aħna (we)",
              "ending": "-na",
              "form": "konna",
              "en": "we were",
              "say": "Aħna konna"
            },
            {
              "person": "Intom (you)",
              "ending": "-tu",
              "form": "kontu",
              "en": "you were",
              "say": "Intom kontu"
            },
            {
              "person": "Huma (they)",
              "ending": "-u",
              "form": "kienu",
              "en": "they were",
              "say": "Huma kienu"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "facts": [
        "kont plus a verb means 'used to'. Kont immur = I used to go. Kont niekol = I used to eat.",
        "kont plus a noun means 'was'. Jien kont ħaddied = I was a blacksmith.",
        "The plural of ħanut is ħwienet, one of the broken plurals from Unit 11."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar12",
      "icon": "📖",
      "title": "Grammar",
      "subtitle": "Il-grammatika: saying you weren't, and asking about the past",
      "intro": "Three things that make kont useful: saying you weren't, saying there was, and asking someone about their own past.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "id": "negative-kont",
          "title": "Saying you weren't: the ma...x wrap",
          "explanation": "You met this wrap with other verbs in Unit 10. Kien takes it too: ma in front, x on the end. Kont (I was) becomes ma kontx (I wasn't).",
          "examples": [
            {
              "mt": "Ma kontx naħdem bħala ħaddied",
              "en": "I did not work as a blacksmith"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Ma kontx immur bit-tramm",
              "en": "I didn't use to go by tram"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Ma kienx hemm ferrovija",
              "en": "There was no railway"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Ma konniex id-dar",
              "en": "We weren't at home"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "kien-hemm",
          "title": "Kien hemm: there was, there were",
          "explanation": "Kien hemm covers both there was and there were. It does not change for the plural. Mind the place name: fil-belt, small b, is in the city, any city. il-Belt with a capital B is Valletta itself, and it takes no preposition.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "mt": "Kien hemm ħanut tal-ħelu f'kull raħal",
              "en": "There was a sweet shop in every village"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Kien hemm ħafna ħwienet fil-belt",
              "en": "There were many shops in the city"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Kien hemm ħafna ħwienet il-Belt Valletta",
              "en": "There were many shops in Valletta"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Ma kienx hemm karozzi",
              "en": "There were no cars"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "asking-past",
          "title": "Asking about the past",
          "explanation": "Put a question word in front of kont and you can ask anyone about their own past.",
          "letters": [
            "fejn, where",
            "kif, how",
            "meta, when",
            "x', what"
          ],
          "examples": [
            {
              "mt": "Fejn kont taħdem?",
              "en": "Where did you work?"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Kif kont tmur għax-xogħol?",
              "en": "How did you go to work?"
            },
            {
              "mt": "X'kont taħdem?",
              "en": "What did you do for work?"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Meta kont hemm?",
              "en": "When were you there?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "g12build",
          "type": "build",
          "max": 4,
          "title": "Build the sentence",
          "items": [
            {
              "mt": "Ma kontx naħdem bħala ħaddied",
              "en": "I did not work as a blacksmith"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Kien hemm ħanut tal-ħelu f'kull raħal",
              "en": "There was a sweet shop in every village"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Fejn kont taħdem?",
              "en": "Where did you work?"
            },
            {
              "mt": "Ma kienx hemm ferrovija",
              "en": "There was no railway"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
